{"chunk_id": "0adeef11e420", "text": "This section recounts how King Dushmanta responds after hearing Sakuntala explain her origin as the adopted daughter of the sage Kanwa, who found her abandoned and protected by birds in the wilderness. Struck by her beauty and dignity, Dushmanta asks her to marry him according to the Gandharva form of marriage\u2014a union based on mutual consent without formal rites. Sakuntala hesitates, wishing her father to give her away, but the king argues from religious law that such a marriage is acceptable for Kshatriyas. She agrees on one condition: the son born of their union must become the heir to his throne. Dushmanta promises and weds her before leaving for his capital. When Kanwa returns, he already knows what happened through spiritual insight and blesses the union, prophesying that their son will become a mighty ruler whose power will extend over the earth.\nDushmanta persuades Sakuntala to a Gandharva marriage, agrees their son will be heir, and Kanwa later approves the secret union, foretelling a mighty son.\nThemes: Gandharva marriage, royal lineage, consent and conditions, ascetic approval, prophecy of future king", "vector": [0.012001690454781055, -0.00020352838328108191, -0.000509971403516829, 0.005100551061332226, -0.03140654042363167, 0.018273627385497093, -0.017497165128588676, -0.016104890033602715, -0.02182125486433506, -0.017992494627833366, 0.012322984635829926, 0.009364397265017033, 0.007650826591998339, 0.007403161842375994, -0.0052377707324922085, 0.012456857599318027, 0.04784611240029335, -0.017925558611750603, 0.018621696159243584, -0.022450456395745277, 0.0066233533434569836, -0.016238762065768242, 0.0031409889925271273, 0.0010952462907880545, -0.02167399413883686, 0.027095841243863106, 0.020469140261411667, -0.016412796452641487, 0.003564361482858658, -0.0004076843033544719, -0.008802131749689579, -0.0021386167500168085, -0.008213091641664505, -0.029800068587064743, -0.028729086741805077, -0.01088385283946991